{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied stdio handler on node1 TCP port 9097 through inetd or xinetd, with one handler process per connection.","status":"satisfied","summary":"BusyBox inetd was installed from EL9-compatible packages, configured with a nowait service invoking the unchanged supplied handler, enabled under systemd, and directly observed listening on TCP 9097. Eight held connections produced exactly eight distinct handler children.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2baf3ff90dda44e8","cmd-b25de63f25f44982","cmd-daa44de01a954fae","cmd-6f10dfe8b8ba44cc","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Return PONG for a newline-terminated PING request and ERROR for other lines.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct clients on node2 validated PING, non-PING, and empty-line responses, including after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1008554c662f43cf","cmd-53d09b42709d42d7","cmd-3a3cb27cd8474a65"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Multiple sequential and concurrent clients must complete, without leaving handler processes behind.","status":"satisfied","summary":"One hundred sequential and 64 concurrent requests passed. A held-connection test showed eight handlers for eight clients, all clients completed, and the handler-child count returned to zero. Forty concurrent requests and zero residual children were also demonstrated after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-840713ba8b3047a7","cmd-0974a6bed96c4e04","cmd-daa44de01a954fae","cmd-e45212113b234eeb","cmd-4f93e5036f324280","cmd-53d09b42709d42d7","cmd-c2b4d0e87f1f447d"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the protocol notes in /srv/legacy2/inetd-request-activation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The protocol.txt SHA-256 hash remained identical to the prepared baseline on both nodes through final and post-restart checks; the supplied handler was likewise unchanged.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-d7e3fdf8f9714162","cmd-1ac8a0984fed4d63","cmd-3a3cb27cd8474a65","cmd-6f10dfe8b8ba44cc"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained AlmaLinux 9.6 on kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 after execution and restart. The installed inetd implementation and Python compatibility package are EL9 packages, and package-health checks remained successful.","evidence_ids":["cmd-80c94096208a40d2","cmd-6b5399387f4e46b0","cmd-1ac8a0984fed4d63","cmd-3a3cb27cd8474a65","cmd-6f10dfe8b8ba44cc","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"All managed-system mutations had a clear role: installing required EL9 software, configuring and exposing the requested service, collecting bounded behavioral evidence, or performing the mandatory restart protocol. No causally unrelated mutation was identified, and final observations show healthy package state and no failed units. Hygiene is reduced because the evidence-supporting client commands left five unneeded artifacts on node2: /tmp/hold_legacy_clients.py, its two log/PID files, and two final-test log/PID files. These remained after execution rather than being cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-41f01c8fba5d4114","cmd-0974a6bed96c4e04","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered system/data/service behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts. The only notable defect is minor retained test residue in node2's /tmp directory.","limitations":[]}
